<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
Spartrak — PDP (Figma 526:21854 / 532:15187 / 534:9322).

Two blocks added, one core block removed, one block re-templated and one
moved. Porto's own catalog_product_view.xml is otherwise left completely
alone: its layout="2columns-right", every <move> it performs, and its custom
blocks all still apply. The Figma PDP is a full-width two-column
page (media 816 | 48 gutter | info 480, inside the 1344 band), and that is
achieved in CSS by re-flowing .column.main rather than by re-cutting the page
layout here — changing layout="2columns-right" to "1column" would orphan
every block Porto moves into sidebar.additional and is a bigger, separate
decision.

  spartrak.pdp.head    goes FIRST inside product.info.media (a core Magento
                       container) for two reasons: it is the earliest point in
                       the PDP's own content, so the temporary inline <style>
                       it carries lands before the styled markup; and being a
                       child of `.product.media` is what lets the Figma media
                       overlay (discount badge 526:23655 + the three round
                       action buttons 526:23305) position itself over the
                       gallery without touching Porto's 528-line gallery.phtml
                       or the Fotorama widget inside it.

  spartrak.pdp.options goes LAST inside product.info.main — the Figma
                       "خيارات المنتج" card (526:23403), which sits below the
                       add-to-cart row.

Both target containers are declared by Magento core, not by Porto, so neither
depends on Porto's layout surviving unchanged.
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <head>
        <!--
          The product page stylesheet: components/_pdp.less,
          components/_reviews.less and the shared section rail the related
          products carousel is built from. Previously part of the
          render-blocking global bundle on every route. See
          web/css/spartrak-pdp.less.
        -->
        <css src="css/spartrak-pdp.css"/>
        <css src="css/spartrak-pdp-video.css"/>
    </head>
    <body>
        <!--
          ===================================================================
          THE SINGLE BIGGEST PERFORMANCE LINE ON THIS PAGE
          ===================================================================
          Magento_ProductVideo adds `product.info.media.video` to every product
          page, unconditionally. Its template is one x-magento-init that
          requires Magento_ProductVideo/js/fotorama-add-video-events, which
          depends on `load-player`, which depends on `vimeoWrapper`, which
          pulls in the entire Vimeo Player SDK.

          MEASURED on this store, on a product with NO videos at all
          (/ar/sp-9055.html, which renders the placeholder image):

              fotorama-add-video-events.min.js   3.5 KB transfer   12.7 KB parsed
              vimeo/player.min.js                5.8 KB            19.4 KB
              vimeo/vimeo-wrapper.min.js         0.4 KB             0.1 KB
              load-player.min.js                 1.6 KB             4.6 KB
              ..................................................................
              4 requests                        11.3 KB            36.8 KB

          Four requests and 36.8 KB of parsed JavaScript on every product page,
          for a feature ~8,900 of this catalogue's products do not use.

          NOTHING IS LOST. Magento_ProductVideo stays enabled and keeps doing
          every other job it has: its admin Add Video dialog, its media-gallery
          entry converter, its save/read handlers, its `video_url` columns on
          the gallery select and its table. Only the STOREFRONT PLAYER is
          replaced — by js/spartrak-pdp-video-mixin.js, which ships inside
          mage/gallery/gallery's existing bundle and requests nothing from a
          provider until a shopper presses play.

          It also fixes a defect core's player has on this store: that one
          matches videos to gallery frames BY ARRAY INDEX
          (fotorama-add-video-events.js:484-486) while
          js/spartrak-gallery-rtl-mixin reverses the frame array for Arabic, so
          its videos attach to the wrong frames here. The mixin reads the
          active frame instead and is immune to the reversal by construction.
        -->
        <referenceBlock name="product.info.media.video" remove="true"/>

        <referenceContainer name="product.info.media">
            <block class="Magento\Catalog\Block\Product\View"
                   name="spartrak.pdp.head"
                   before="-"
                   template="Magento_Catalog::product/view/spartrak-pdp.phtml"/>
        </referenceContainer>
        <referenceContainer name="product.info.main">
            <block class="Magento\Catalog\Block\Product\View"
                   name="spartrak.pdp.options"
                   after="-"
                   template="Magento_Catalog::product/view/spartrak-options.phtml"/>
        </referenceContainer>

        <move
            element="catalog.product.related"
            destination="content"
            after="product.info.details"/>

        <!--
          RELATED PRODUCTS — Figma 535:12047 (desktop) / 655:19767 (mobile).

          The <move> above is what makes the block render at all. This only
          changes how it LOOKS: the class and the template. The block is still
          Magento's own related-products block, so what it shows stays exactly
          what an admin picked under a product's "Related Products" tab, in
          their order — and the template it now points at is the SAME rail the
          homepage renders (same header partial, same card, same CSS, same
          carousel widget).

          `limit` caps how many cards reach the HTML; related products are
          unbounded in the admin, and forty linked products would otherwise be
          forty cards, images and add-to-cart forms in the PDP's response.
          Changing it is this one line, no PHP.
        -->
        <referenceBlock name="catalog.product.related"
                        class="Spartrak\Catalog\Block\Product\RelatedRail"
                        template="Spartrak_Catalog::product/related-rail.phtml">
            <arguments>
                <argument name="limit" xsi:type="number">12</argument>
            </arguments>
        </referenceBlock>
    </body>
</page>
